{"created": "2026-10-07T04:54:17.591002+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-10T21:27:07.249789+00:00", "id": 23203270, "conceptrecid": "23203269", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23203270", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23203269", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203270", "metadata": {"title": "An explicit complex polynomial retract in five variables: a consequence of affine-space cancellation failure", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23203270", "publication_date": "2026-10-06", "description": "Using OpenAI's explicit complex cancellation fourfold, this consequence note gives split complex-algebra maps and a five-component idempotent polynomial endomorphism of affine five-space whose image has transcendence degree four and is not a polynomial algebra. The cylinder-to-retract implication is classical, as recorded by Nagamine; the cancellation example, stabilization and nonpolynomiality are attributed to OpenAI. The four-variable retract question is not settled. The package includes exact symbolic certificates, written dependency audits and a bounded priority audit. The actual Lean sources were inspected, but a full kernel build was not reproduced; no formal verification of the follow-on theorem is claimed. AI tools were used extensively in research, drafting and verification. This preprint has not undergone conventional human peer review/refereeing; automated reviews are not human peer review. The original note and new verification artifacts are CC BY4.0; the bundled OpenAI Lean sources and adapted build configuration/audit harness retain Apache2.0.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["Costa retract question", "polynomial retracts", "affine-space cancellation", "complex affine geometry", "idempotent polynomial map", "algebra retracts", "retracts of polynomial rings", "Zariski cancellation problem", "complex affine five-space", "polynomial cylinder", "smooth affine varieties", "locally nilpotent derivations", "split algebra homomorphisms", "exact symbolic verification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/openai/math/tree/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-explicit-failure-of-complex-affine-space-cancellation-September-23-2026", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.1811.04153", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23203269"}}]}}, "title": "An explicit complex polynomial retract in five variables: a consequence of affine-space cancellation failure", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203270", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203270", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203270?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203270", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203270", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23203270", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203270/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203269", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203269", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203269", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23203269", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203270/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203270/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203270/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203270/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203270:paper.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203270:paper.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203270:paper.pd